From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 14:41:57 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 02/42] multitenant: tests for Manager concurrency, eviction,
 error retry

Nine tests covering the Manager invariants that the spike doesn't
exercise directly:

  - concurrent Acquire on the same tenant loads exactly once (initOnce)
  - eviction respects refcount: pinned tenants block until released
  - loader errors propagate and the entry is forgotten so a future
    Acquire actually retries the loader
  - Shutdown rejects new Acquires (ErrManagerClosed) and tears down
    all loaded runtimes
  - Handle.Release is idempotent
  - CachedVKResolver expires entries after the configured TTL

Passes under -race in ~1.2s.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
